darkzilla: enable native Windows dark mode (follows the system setting).

Call wxApp::MSWEnableDarkMode() in OnInit() before any windows are created.
The default flag (DarkMode_Auto) follows the Windows light/dark setting.
While dark mode is active, re-enable wxWidgets' own static box painting:
OnInit() disables it and wxWidgets >= 3.3.3 leaves the label to the native
group box control, which has no dark theme and paints it black.

Derived from Pharaoh2k/FileZilla-Themed-For-Windows (GPLv3+).

diff --git a/src/interface/FileZilla.cpp b/src/interface/FileZilla.cpp
--- a/src/interface/FileZilla.cpp
+++ b/src/interface/FileZilla.cpp
@@ -190,6 +190,21 @@
 	AddStartupProfileRecord("CFileZillaApp::OnInit(): Loading options"sv);
 	options_ = std::make_unique<COptions>();
 
+#ifdef __WXMSW__
+	// darkzilla: enable wxWidgets' native dark mode, following the Windows
+	// system setting (wxApp::DarkMode_Auto). Must run before any windows
+	// are created. Requires wxWidgets >= 3.3.
+	MSWEnableDarkMode();
+
+	// darkzilla: the native group box control has no dark theme and paints
+	// its label black; wxWidgets >= 3.3.3 no longer gives static boxes an
+	// explicit foreground colour that would switch them back to custom
+	// painting. The optimized-paint option was disabled above; re-enable it
+	// when dark mode is active so labels use the dark-mode text colour.
+	if (wxSystemSettings::GetAppearance().IsDark())
+		wxSystemOptions::SetOption(_T("msw.staticbox.optimized-paint"), 1);
+#endif
+
 	InitLocale();
 
 #ifndef _DEBUG
